PART 4 -- THE VERDICTS
====================================================================================================
  V1 THE BUDGET'S CANDIDATE SINKS: (a) THE ORBITAL HALO -- the outer orbits' per-tracer specific j from the G209 profile's outer bins is 4.2-6.7 x j_infall (E2 primary; E1 agrees): amplitude-sufficing, concentrated where the caustic sheet's tangential speed carries j_infall (r_dep = 1.73 R500 -- where the measured f jumps 0.10 -> 0.76); (b) THE TIDAL CONVERSION -- the quadrupole capacity is 3.6% of the missing at the t_H upper bound (e_N = 0.71 at the turnaround, differential 2.55e-02): SUBSIDIARY, not the sink; (c) THE MERGER/ACCRETION -- the parent reservoir's own j = 6.2 x j_infall at R_ta (LSS bulk ~24 x): the delocalization register.
  V2 THE OUTER-J MEASUREMENT: the outer shell [1,5) R500 (5733 members, 58 clusters) shows an amplitude excess +14.2 +- 5.0 km/s per R500 (z = +2.85); v_rot,los = 36.8 +- 12.9 km/s -> THE OUTER-J NUMBER: j_outer = 6.654e+04 +- 2.337e+04 kpc.km/s (f_outer = 0.39 +- 0.14, UL 0.67).  Per-bin 91%-coverage: f(2-3) = 0.76 +- 0.19 (z = +3.96; trials p = 4.5e-04), f(3-5) = 1.27 +- 0.32 (z = +4.00; trials p = 3.7e-04); f(1-1.5) = 0.06 +- 0.16, f(1.5-2) = 0.10 +- 0.21; axes uniform (Rayleigh |z| <= 1.34); the stack's coherent vector is null-consistent (5.3 vs 7.4 km/s/R500) -- the deposit is per-cluster oriented by construction of 58 independent infall axes.
  V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT -- the number that closes S4's open end: the infall's angular momentum is NOT missing: it is DEPOSITED IN THE OUTER HALO at j_outer-class = 1.29e+05-2.17e+05 kpc.km/s (the 2-3 and 3-5 R500 shells' per-cluster ordered kinematics carry f = 0.76 +- 0.19 and 1.27 +- 0.32 of j_infall, bracketing the missing 91% = 1.55e+05; the deposit materializes at r_dep = sqrt(3) R500 as the framework's caustic geometry predicts; the core's isotropy stands as the static equilibrium's signature, closing S4's thread with f_core + f_outer = 0.48 +- 0.15 (2-5 R500, per-bin: 0.85, 1.36).  The honest caveats are registered: per-cluster AMPLITUDE statistic (the net stack spin is ~0 because 58 infall orientations average on the sky -- not a missing deposit), the streaming-vs-rotation degeneracy of the LOS projection (both are the envelope's j-carrying kinematics), the 6-shell trials factor (2-3 and 3-5 stay >~3 sigma), and the tidal channel capacity-subsidiary (3.6%) -- the residual, if any is demanded, is the parent sample's own 6.2x budget (the merger/accretion delocalization).
